RESULT: castling rights are a CONDITIONER, NOT the sole discriminator.

  pos 1: rights -> BAIL, stripped -> BAIL        (castling made no difference)
  pos 4: rights -> BAIL, stripped -> BAIL        (castling made no difference)
  pos 7: rights -> 11,390 nodes, stripped -> BAIL (castling made ALL the difference)

So my earlier sentence 'the bail fires on positions with no castling rights and not when rights are present'
is REFUTED as a general rule by positions 1 and 4, which bail WITH rights.

What survives:
  - REMOVING castling rights never PREVENTED a bail (3 of 3 stripped cells bailed);
  - HAVING rights sometimes prevents it (pos 7) and sometimes does not (pos 1, pos 4).
So rights are necessary-for-searching on some boards and irrelevant on others, which means at least one
FURTHER factor is involved and castling rights alone cannot be the answer.
